      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "In the past you could \"Show avatar\" and then change it back to \"Use safety settings\" to show the avatar up to the point when that user changes the avatar.\n\nHowever apparently that was a bug and now it changes it back to the option you selected.\n\nI was about to write a feature request to change it back to what it was before, but your suggestions is better.\n\nI would prefer that the temporary show avatar is reset after you exit the game, because then you don't have to re-enable it everytime you change the instance (for example: when you are world hopping and that user joins that).",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-06-19T15:16:44.084Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When you go around public worlds you meet a lot of people!\nIt's nice to have the show avatar button for friends and people you know really well.\nBut for people you just met and might not meet ever again it would be nice to have a temporary show avatar button that goes back to the safety option once you leave the instance or exit the game.\nThis would give more safety and performance incase one of the randoms you've shown decide to randomly join you at a later date or by chance in a public world but with an avatar that is not performance friendly or an avatar that is malicious.",
